2	/**
3	 * scout-block.cjs - Cross-platform hook for blocking directory access
4	 *
5	 * Blocks access to directories listed in the shipped .claude/.ckignore baseline
6	 * plus an optional project-local .claude/.ckignore override at the git root.
7	 * Uses gitignore-spec compliant pattern matching via 'ignore' package
8	 *
9	 * Blocking Rules:
10	 * - File paths: Blocks any file_path/path/pattern containing blocked directories
11	 * - Bash commands: Blocks directory access (cd, ls, cat, etc.) but ALLOWS build commands
12	 *   - Blocked: cd node_modules, ls packages/web/node_modules, cat dist/file.js
13	 *   - Allowed: npm build, go build, cargo build, make, mvn, gradle, docker build, kubectl, terraform
14	 *
15	 * Configuration:
16	 * - Edit .claude/.ckignore to customize shipped baseline patterns
17	 * - Add <project-root>/.claude/.ckignore to override locally without changing the baseline
18	 * - Supports negation patterns (!) to allow specific paths
19	 *
20	 * Exit Codes:
21	 * - 0: Command allowed
22	 * - 2: Command blocked
23	 *
24	 * Core logic extracted to lib/scout-checker.cjs for OpenCode plugin reuse.
25	 */
